        "id": 37431
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T09:22:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it can overwrite the value by LMh and imho we should do. mi_thermal updates the thermal pressure caused by software policy while LMh updates the same pressure caused by hardware LMh throttling. Both mechanisms update the pressure through arch_set_thermal_pressure either independently or cumulatively, and the scheduler will comprehensively process the combined thermal pressure signals from both sources? In practice, cpufreq_cooling.c updates the pressure after freq_qos_update_request calling, but mi_thermal driver just calls freq_qos and does nothing thereafter.",
      "parentUuid": "5ea637e9_fa15e209",
      "revId": "05cca4ce5395c88e47a70112ecd8172d39d55091",
      "serverId": "1ec6b3db-b2c1-4fa4-84a2-4c7efe89ba71"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4d105d2_3d710623",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
